,"github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1295#issuecomment-279814054"},"message":"re API -- counter example is \"git annex initremote\" which allows for all the varieties without creating initremote-TYPE for each one of them.  I do hear you that it might be trick(ier) to implement given us trying to fulfill both cmdline and Python interfaces, but it is not completely impossible.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487101993,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTgxNjY5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1295#issuecomment-279816693"},"message":"re --shared, I guess there is some dichotomy from documented and actual in git:\n```\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=all; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects\nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n2\ndrwxrwsr-x 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:48 .git/objects/\n\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects   \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrws--- 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:48 .git/objects/\n\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=0x731; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrws--- 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:49 .git/objects/\n```\nso it looks like it doesn't give too much about having explicit permissions specified?  more over doc says:\n```\n       core.sharedRepository\n           When group (or true), the repository is made shareable between several users in a group (making sure all the files and objects are\n           group-writable). When all (or world or everybody), the repository will be readable by all users, additionally to being group-shareable.\n           When umask (or false), Git will use permissions reported by umask(2). When 0xxx, where 0xxx is an octal number, files in the repository\n           will have this mode value.  0xxx will override user’s umask value (whereas the other options will only override requested parts of the\n           user’s umask value). Examples: 0660 will make the repo read/write-able for the owner and group, but inaccessible to others (equivalent to\n           group unless umask is e.g.  0022).  0640 is a repository that is group-readable but not group-writable. See git-init(1). False by\n           default.\n```\nand is just or'ing inverse of umask for any setting:\n```shell\n(git)hopa:/tmp/test[master]\n$\u003e umask 000\n2 12046.....................................:Tue 14 Feb 2017 02:51:31 PM EST:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/test[master]\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=0x660; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects\nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrwsrwx 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:51 .git/objects/\n2 12047.....................................:Tue 14 Feb 2017 02:51:33 PM EST:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/test[master]\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=0x640; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrwsrwx 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:51 .git/objects/\n2 12048.....................................:Tue 14 Feb 2017 02:51:39 PM EST:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/test[master]\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects      \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrwsrwx 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:51 .git/objects/\n2 12049.....................................:Tue 14 Feb 2017 02:51:45 PM EST:.\n(git)hopa:/tmp/test[master]\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=all; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n2\ndrwxrwsrwx 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 14 14:51 .git/objects/\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487215720,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDIyMDkwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1295#issuecomment-280220902"},"message":"I guess it might please @mih, added edit 3  to the original post ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487268537,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDQxMDg0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1295#issuecomment-280410848"},"message":"Re `--shared`: Just from looking at what you did and the man page you posted:\nDid you notice that they are talking about `0640` where you pass `0x640`? I'd expect it to work, too, but might be worth trying ...\n\nEdit: For me (git 2.7.0) it works that way indeed .. ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487275703,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDQ0NDE2NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1295#issuecomment-280444164"},"message":"great catch @bpoldrack ! ;)\n```shell\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=0x640; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects\nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n1\ndrwxrws--- 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 16 15:07 .git/objects/\n\n$\u003e builtin cd /tmp; rm -rf test; mkdir test; cd test; git init --shared=0640; git config --get core.sharedrepository; ls -ld .git/objects                 \nInitialized empty shared Git repository in /tmp/test/.git/\n0640\ndrwxr-s--- 4 yoh yoh 80 Feb 16 15:07 .git/objects/\n```\nso we can just pass over the core.sharedrepository value into the call","files":null},{"type":4,"a